    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass and the build succeeds. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the household-duplicate rejection rule for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**The rule:** creating an owner is rejected with **409 Conflict** when another owner already has the same `lastName` *and* the same `address` \u2014 compared case-insensitively and with whitespace collapsed (trimmed, internal runs reduced to a single space). A request bypasses the rule by setting `sharesHousehold: true`.\n\n**Changes**, following the existing `DuplicateTelephone` feature as the model:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a request-only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `OwnerFields` schema so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` exposes the flag.\n\n2. **`DuplicateHouseholdException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 a new `@ExceptionHandler` mapping `DuplicateHouseholdException` to a 409 `ProblemDetail`.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added `rejectDuplicateHousehold(...)` to the existing `prepareNewOwner` intake pipeline. It returns early when `sharesHousehold` is true; otherwise it compares the collapsed/case-insensitive `lastName` + `address` against all existing owners and throws when a clash is found. A small `collapseWhitespace` helper handles trimming/collapsing (null-safe).\n\nThe three acceptance tests all pass: rejects same lastName+address (409), allows a different address, and allows the duplicate when `sharesHousehold` is true.",
