    "probe_text": "The POST `/api/owners` endpoint is handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)` (implementing `OwnersApi`, mapped at `/api` + `/owners`). Here is everything that happens, in order, from the request arriving to the response being built.\n\n## 1. Authorization (before the method runs)\n- **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403 (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:105`).\n\n## 2. Bean Validation on the request body (before the method body)\nThe API interface declares `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (`OwnersApi.java:86`), so Jakarta Bean Validation runs on the DTO first; any violation yields a 400 (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`) before `addOwner`'s code executes:\n- **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(min=1,max=30)`\n- **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(min=1,max=30)`\n- **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(min=1,max=255)`\n- **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(min=1,max=80)`\n- **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[-0-9()+.\\s]*$)`, `@Size(min=1,max=20)`\n- **email** (optional) \u2014 `@Size(min=1,max=255)`, `@Email` (only enforced when present)\n\n## 3. Method body \u2014 `prepareNewOwner(ownerFieldsDto)` (`:226`), in this order:\n1. **`validateRequiredFields`** (`:259`) \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank (whitespace-only counts as blank). Any missing \u2192 `RequiredFieldsMissingException` (400 with an `errors` array).\n2. **`normalizeTelephone`** (side-effect) (`:290`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets, applies E.164 form (keeps `+`/country code if present, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`), and **writes the normalized value back into the DTO**. Must match `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`, else `InvalidFieldsException(\"telephone\")` (400).\n3. **`normalizeEmail`** (side-effect) (`:326`) \u2014 `null` is allowed (email is optional); when present it is trimmed, must match the email pattern (else `InvalidFieldsException(\"email\")`, 400), and is **lower-cased and written back into the DTO**.\n4. **`rejectDuplicateTelephone`** (`:346`) \u2014 loads all owners and rejects if the normalized telephone already equals any existing owner's telephone \u2192 `DuplicateTelephoneException` (409).\n5. **`rejectDuplicateHousehold`** (`:366`) \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold == true` (opt-out), loads all owners and rejects if the same `lastName` + `address` already exist (compared case-insensitively with collapsed/trimmed whitespace) \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` (409).\n\n## 4. Remaining side-effects in `addOwner` (`:107`), in order:\n1. Map the (now normalized) DTO to an `Owner` entity via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.\n2. **Default the registration date** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is null, set it to `LocalDate.now()` (`:111`).\n3. **Assign a customer code** \u2014 `setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(lastName))`, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` where `NNNN` = `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits (`:114`, `:244`).\n4. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (`ClinicServiceImpl.java:234`).\n5. Map the saved entity back to `OwnerDto`, set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, and return **201 Created** (`:116`).\n\n### Notes\n- Steps 2 and 3 in section 3 mutate the incoming DTO in place; the normalized telephone/email are what get mapped, persisted, and returned.\n- Uniqueness checks (duplicate telephone, duplicate household, and the customer-code sequence) each independently call `findAllOwners()`, and none of this is done under a single `@Transactional` guard on `addOwner`, so the checks are read-then-write with no locking."
  },
